   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Making an inference",
     "texto": [
      "When you work something out from clues or from the context, use **-나 보다** (it seems that, must be): 가다 → **갔나 봐요** (it seems (he/she) went), 비가 오다 → **비가 왔나 봐요** (it seems it rained), 아프다 → **아픈가 봐요** (it seems (he/she) is ill). The clue does not have to be something you saw directly.",
      "안나 씨가 아직 안 **왔나 봐요** = it seems Anna has not arrived yet."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Depending on the form",
     "texto": [
      "With verbs you use **-나 보다**, with adjectives **-(으)ㄴ가 보다**, and with nouns **-인가 보다**.",
      "피곤**한가 봐요** = it seems (he/she) is tired. 학생**인가 봐요** = it seems (he/she) is a student."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
